+# Concurrent direct-tcpip channel opens (fork extension)
+
+This branch extends official libssh2 1.11.1. Existing APIs and their behavior
+remain available. The extension permits multiple SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN requests
+to be in flight on one authenticated session. It does not make a session thread
+safe: all calls for a session must be serialized on its owning event loop.
+
+1. Set the session nonblocking and complete authentication.
+2. `libssh2_channel_direct_tcpip_begin` copies the target and origin and returns
+   an opaque `LIBSSH2_CHANNEL_OPEN *`, without I/O. NULL indicates an allocation
+   or argument error (see session_last_errno).
+3. Call `libssh2_channel_open_poll(op, &channel)` for each pending operation.
+   EAGAIN retains the operation. **Every other result consumes it.** Zero
+   transfers the established channel to the caller, to use/free with existing
+   channel APIs. Negative results leave `channel` NULL. Invalid API arguments
+   (NULL op/output) return BAD_USE without consuming anything.
+4. `libssh2_channel_open_cancel(op)` marks cancellation. Continue polling until
+   a terminal result. An operation cancelled before its first poll is discarded.
+   A partially sent OPEN
+   must finish sending the same packet. A sent OPEN retains its channel ID until
+   the peer rejects it, or confirms it and the channel is closed. Cancellation
+   completes with CHANNEL_CLOSED, or CHANNEL_FAILURE for a late rejection.
+5. Freeing the session releases all remaining operations, including requests
+   whose peers never reply. All outstanding operation pointers then become
+   invalid. As with other libssh2 APIs, retry session_free if it returns EAGAIN.
+
+Replies are dispatched by recipient channel ID before subsequent channel data
+is processed. Partial transport writes retain stable packet storage; other
+operations cannot overtake an incomplete transport packet. This ordering does
+not serialize server confirmation waits. Legacy packet waiters continue waiting
+when a reply belongs to a different operation.
+
+The caller implements timeouts and admission limits. After timing out a single
+open, cancel it and retain its cleanup operation, without closing healthy
+channels. Never free or reuse its channel ID prematurely. Bound the total
+number of outstanding operations, including cancelled requests awaiting replies.
+A transport/protocol error requires session teardown, not retrying that session.
+
+`test_channel_open` is a standalone static-library test covering multiple OPENs
+before replies, out-of-order success/failure, partial send/EAGAIN, cancellation
+before and after send, late confirmation/close, malformed replies, and allocator
+balance during session teardown. ProxyLane's real SSH fixture additionally
+withholds server confirmations while later channels exchange data on the same
+authenticated transport.
